status  (again-closed, after the build) Built 1 part, RangeBox_r2_Layout, RangeBox_r2_Carrier_Carrier and RangeBox_r2.SLDASM, reusing the 4 parts already built; no interference between the gears in any mode, where they stand. Its turning gears are mated to turn in each of its 3 modes, one configuration each (H, N and L), and SolidWorks reports no mate in error in any of them: it opens in H; to switch mode, double-click another mode's configuration in SolidWorks' ConfigurationManager. Drag Sun in SolidWorks and the rest of its train follow. RangeSlv slides along Output, to its place in each mode. The 3 copies of Planet turn on Carrier, and RangeBox_r2_Carrier_Carrier holds Carrier's axes and planes only: a plate and pins are yours to add. Ring stays fixed where it is placed: its shaft does not turn. A turn you give the gears in one mode can show in other modes, so a dog can stand across its sleeve in another; to put the gears back there, press Update SolidWorks with that mode showing. 1 thing to do by hand: Assign a material to SunGear; the build leaves it unset. RangeBox.SLDASM was not open in SolidWorks, so it was not read again; as read at 02:52, your Sprocket-3, Sprocket-4, Sprocket-1, 2 other components and 8 mates stay in RangeBox.SLDASM, and your User Keyway Sketch and User Keyway stay in Gear_m1.25_N29, which Sun's new part replaces; RangeBox_r2 has none of them, nor anything added since.
